.TH BOOTSTASH-PROVISION-GOOGLE 8 "September 2026" "bootstash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bootstash-provision-google \- write Google OIDC client keys into /etc/bootstash/oidc-google
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bootstash provision-google
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-secrets\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-origin\fR \fIurl\fR]
[\fB\-project\fR \fIid\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the exact OIDC redirect URI
.RB ( $PUBLIC_ORIGIN/oidc/callback )
and Google Auth Platform console URLs, then writes the Client ID and
Client secret you paste to
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google
(mode
.BR 0640 ,
.BR root:bootstash ).
It does not edit
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.PP
It does
.B not
create the Google OAuth web client.
.B gcloud
has no supported command for that client type. Consent / branding is
once per GCP project. One web client per
.BR PUBLIC_ORIGIN .
If
.B gcloud
is on
.BR PATH ,
the current project id is used for console links.
It does not create Unix users.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Operator config to read
.B PUBLIC_ORIGIN
from. Default:
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-secrets " path"
File to write. Default:
.IR /etc/bootstash/oidc-google .
.TP
.BI \-origin " url"
.B PUBLIC_ORIGIN
if it is not already in
.IR /etc/default/bootstash .
.TP
.BI \-project " id"
GCP project id for console URLs when
.B gcloud
has none.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bootstash (8),
.BR bootstash (5)
